Next steps:

1. Run the migration:
     bin/rails db:migrate

2. Generate module-wise permissions from your existing routes:
     bin/rails argus_trail:fetch_permissions

   Re-run it any time you add controllers/actions — it only ever adds new
   permissions. `bin/rails argus_trail:fetch_permissions:prune` removes ones
   whose route is gone and that aren't granted to any role.

3. Gate your own controllers behind a permission with one line — no further
   code needed, the required permission is derived from the controller and
   action automatically:

     class AccountsController < ApplicationController
       include Argus::Trail::Authorizable
     end

4. Visit the mounted engine (default /admin/access, see config/routes.rb) to
   create roles, assign permissions, and assign roles to actors. With
   neither Pundit policies nor config.authorize_with set, the admin screens
   are open to any signed-in actor — define
   Argus::Trail::RolePolicy/PermissionPolicy/AuditEntryPolicy (Pundit) or set
   config.authorize_with to restrict further (e.g. to admins only).

Want to customize the HTML? Run:
     bin/rails generate argus:trail:views
to copy the views into app/views/argus/trail for editing.
